      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The current HUD display makes it difficult to tell whether sound is being produced or not.\nAudio systems are generally unstable, and it is common to lose my voice in the microphone. I would like to see a clearer indication of whether the voice is coming in or not, as shown in the following video.\n![](https://www.youtube.com/embed/FiMT1ueRyts)\nRelated: [Muting/Unmuting when pasting URLs with Ctrl+V | Voters | VRChat](https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/mutingunmuting-when-pasting-urls-with-ctrlv)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-04-14T21:42:45.346Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Its gonna sound crazy but Im gonna throw it out there. Those of us who game at night have a hard time remembering or being able to tell when we get too loud. What if we had a toggleable HUD of a bar with a range slider indicator that showed the volume we are currently talking at? Like a whisper would be down near the blue end of the bar, green would be good volume near the middle, and red would be at the far end in the \"too loud\" range. Its just a visual indicator for yourself to see when you are talking if you are in the red so you can quiet down. It doesnt control your mic or anything, its just a noise meter for reminder convenience in regards of your real environment, not the game volume.",
